  "decision": "Keep the product default batch size at 16. Batch 64 is a demonstrated sensitivity setting for this delayed workload, with slower immediate-feedback promotion and unresolved erroneous-label adoption. No production learner/prior/quality/pending setting was changed.",
  "algorithm_interpretation": [
    "Cold-start requires 20 measured families per arm before posterior-based expansion; low 10% allocation combined with a 16-member closed-cohort feedback barrier limits candidate evidence under long delay.",
    "The development delayed TS run leaves a mean 1018.375 arrivals unenrolled, of which 934.5625 wait for cohort feedback and 83.8125 wait for reconciliation.",
    "Increasing the existing cohort size alone improves synthetic throughput; no pending outcome is imputed and the quality/publication gates remain intact.",
    "Fewer harmful adoptions do not eliminate wrong-label risk. Trial and deployment exposures are reported separately.",
    "The simulation now follows production staging of a promotion proposal for an open cohort while checking that no adoption occurs."
  ],
  "references": [
    {
      "title": "Thompson Sampling with Unrestricted Delays",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.12431",
      "use": "TS can update from arriving feedback under its stated stochastic delay assumptions; our cohort barrier is an additional design choice. The paper does not establish guarantees for our NIG multi-metric posterior, revised rubrics or informative missingness."
    },
    {
      "title": "Online Learning under Delayed Feedback",
      "url": "https://proceedings.mlr.press/v28/joulani13.html",
      "use": "Background on separating action count from received feedback in delayed online learning."
    }
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Historical canonical-trajectory reference review and judge calibration remain unavailable.",
    "Changing or adapting cohort admission requires further outcome-dependent delay/missingness and actual serving validation; the sensitivity experiment does not implement that change.",
    "Late erroneous rewards still cause harmful adoption under both batch sizes."
  ]
}
